\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Canonical causal DAG for identification. The direct path $L \to Y$ corresponds to the regression coefficient $\beta $ in $Y_{it} = \alpha _i + \gamma _t + \beta L_{it} + \varepsilon _{it}$. The red dashed backdoor path $L \leftarrow S \to Y$ represents confounding by national shocks ($\gamma _t$), which must be blocked by including year fixed effects. The blue path $U \to Y$ represents variance inflation from urban concentration, affecting $\operatorname  {Var}(Y_{it})$ and the leverage of high-luminosity regions. This DAG integrates all confounding and leverage mechanisms discussed in the identification argument.}}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dag_ntl_identification}{{5}{7}{}{}{}}
